# case: 770-playwright-deps-present
# what: the Playwright build layer runs, records its version marker, and installs
#       NOTHING -- `install-deps` is replaced by a no-op while everything around
#       it stays truthful. This is the state the image was in before this layer
#       existed, and the state a project would be in if the layer were ever made
#       conditional on something that is not PLAYWRIGHT_VERSION.
#
#       IT DEFEATS THE DISCRIMINATING ASSERTION, NOT THE CHEAP ONE. The obvious
#       patch -- flipping the `-n "$PLAYWRIGHT_VERSION"` guard to something never
#       true -- would make the case fail at assertion 1 ("the version marker
#       could not be read") and it_finish there, never reaching the dpkg check
#       that is the point of the case. That demonstrates the marker file, not the
#       oracle. 735 learned this the expensive way: its first version targeted
#       gcc, applied cleanly, and case 730 passed all six assertions anyway. A
#       patch a case survives, or that a case fails for a DIFFERENT reason than
#       the one named, demonstrates nothing.
#
#       Leaving the marker write intact is therefore deliberate: assertion 1 must
#       still PASS, so the failures that arrive are unambiguously 2 and 3.
#
#       Expected, in order: assertion 1 PASSes (the version marker is readable),
#       assertion 2 FAILs reporting all ten packages missing and listing them,
#       and assertion 3 FAILs through its dependency-unsatisfied branch.
#
#       Deliberately NOT quoting those three messages verbatim. A header that
#       reproduces text a human is meant to compare against goes stale the moment
#       the message is reworded -- which is exactly what happened to an earlier
#       version of this block, and the same drift the paragraph below avoids by
#       pointing at the case header instead of restating its derivation. Read the
#       current wording in the case; what matters here is WHICH assertion fails
#       and why, not its punctuation.
#
#       Assertion 3 must reach its DEPENDENCY branch, not its unclassified one:
#       an unclassified FAIL would mean the probe never ran (no network, no npx)
#       and would demonstrate nothing about this layer.
#
#       ALL TEN GO MISSING, and that was measured rather than assumed: a
#       simulated install of every other apt-installing layer that SURVIVES into
#       the finished image (249 packages) contains none of the ten. The case's
#       own header carries that derivation in full, including the two caveats it
#       depends on -- libnss3/libnspr4 are transitively reachable through the
#       pyenv layer and are absent only because the cleanup purge reclaims
#       libxmlsec1-dev, and fonts-liberation is absent only because apt picks the
#       first alternative of fontconfig-config's Depends. Read it there rather
#       than trusting this summary: if either caveat stops holding, this patch
#       still applies and still mutates the image, but two of the ten stop
#       discriminating and the demonstration gets quietly weaker.
#
#       ASSERTION 3'S FAILURE MESSAGE IS INDIRECT, EXPECTED, AND NOT A DEFECT.
#       The layer clears /var/lib/apt/lists in BOTH the mutated and unmutated
#       forms (that line is outside this hunk), so in the mutated image
#       `install-deps --dry-run` reaches apt with no package lists and reports
#       `has no installation candidate` rather than `Missing system
#       dependencies`. Both are exit 1 and both are correct: the deps are not
#       there. Measured on the unmutated image, the same empty apt lists produce
#       `All system dependencies are installed.` and exit 0, because Playwright
#       consults dpkg first and never reaches apt when nothing is missing -- so
#       the empty lists do not make assertion 3 vacuous in the passing direction.
#
#       NEEDS A REBUILD. This patch changes an image build input, so the
#       `mutate.sh apply` + `run.sh --reuse-image` procedure in AGENTS.md is
#       SILENTLY WRONG for it -- the image would predate the mutation, the case
#       would pass, and the mutation would be recorded dead having never been
#       applied to anything. patch_needs_rebuild() selects it automatically;
#       demonstrate it with tests/integration/demonstrate-needs-rebuild.sh.
#
#       Safe to demonstrate alongside its neighbours: unlike 735, this layer
#       installs nothing 730/740/750/760 depend on, so it cannot mask them.
#
diff --git a/Dockerfile b/Dockerfile
--- a/Dockerfile
+++ b/Dockerfile
@@ -371,7 +371,7 @@
 ARG PLAYWRIGHT_VERSION=
 RUN if [ -n "$PLAYWRIGHT_VERSION" ]; then \
       apt-get update && \
-      npx --yes "playwright@${PLAYWRIGHT_VERSION}" install-deps && \
+      true "install-deps defeated by mutation 770" && \
       npx --yes "playwright@${PLAYWRIGHT_VERSION}" --version \
         | awk 'NR==1{print $NF}' > /etc/ai-containers-playwright-version && \
       test -s /etc/ai-containers-playwright-version && \
